{"evidence":{"id":"E1","kind":"fact","text":"revenue for fiscal year ending 2014-12-31 = $3,084.4M (XBRL tag SalesRevenueGoodsNet)","source":"10-K accession 0001336917-15-000006, filed 2015-02-20"},"origins":{"queries":[{"sql":"SELECT * FROM veritas_pg.facts WHERE cik = 1336917 ORDER BY fy_end, CASE concept WHEN 'revenue' THEN 0 WHEN 'cogs' THEN 1 WHEN 'sga' THEN 2 WHEN 'depreciation' THEN 3 WHEN 'net_income' THEN 4 WHEN 'cfo' THEN 5 WHEN 'receivables' THEN 6 WHEN 'current_assets' THEN 7 WHEN 'ppe' THEN 8 WHEN 'assets' THEN 9 WHEN 'current_liabilities' THEN 10 WHEN 'lt_debt' THEN 11 ELSE 99 END","rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2014-12-31","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueGoodsNet","value":"3084370000","accn":"0001336917-15-000006","filed":"2015-02-20"}],"mode":"zetaris","label":"executed on Zetaris","table":"facts"}],"rows":[{"cik":"1336917","company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2014-12-31","concept":"revenue","tag":"SalesRevenueGoodsNet","value":"3084370000","accn":"0001336917-15-000006","filed":"2015-02-20"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","fy_end":"2015-12-31","activeRevision":"ac7482310bc9","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001336917-15-000006","filed":"2015-02-20","cik":1336917,"company":"Under Armour","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1336917/000133691715000006/0001336917-15-000006-index.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":1,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue grew 28.5% driven by North America (+$659.3M), International (+$185.4M), and Connected Fitness (+$34.2M) demand.","numbers_show":"Revenue rose $878.9M (28.5%) with consistent quarterly growth (Q1 +25.5%, Q2 +28.5%, Q3 +28.4%, Q4 +30.8%). Segment totals match the cited drivers.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E13","E1","E43","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":1,"findingIndex":3,"management_says":"Revenue growth is attributed to demand drivers; shipment timing is only cited for receivables/cash flow, not for revenue.","numbers_show":"The Q4 receivables spike (DSO 28→34) implies roughly 6 extra days of sales in year-end receivables. On Q4 revenue of $1,170.7M, that equals ~$65–78M of revenue potentially pulled forward into 2015 (7–9% of the $878.9M total growth). The bulk of growth remains demand-driven.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E30","E13","E1","E43","E50"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":0,"management_says":"Revenue growth of 28.5% was driven by North America (+$659.3M), International (+$185.4M), and Connected Fitness (+$34.2M).","numbers_show":"Segment revenues add to the $878.9M total increase; North America grew 23.6%, International 69%, Connected Fitness 178%.","fit":"fits","evidence":["E13","E1","E43","E25"],"verdict":"explanation fits the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":1,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"fits","reason":"Revenue increased $878.9M (28.5%) from $3,084.4M to $3,963.3M. Segment breakdown in MD&A shows North America +$659.3M, International +$185.4M, Connected Fitness +$34.2M, summing to the total increase. Quarterly growth rates are consistent (Q1 +25.5%, Q2 +28.5%, Q3 +28.4%, Q4 +30.8%), supporting broad-based demand rather than a one-time event.","evidence":["E1","E13","E43","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"Revenue growth of 28.5% is driven by genuine demand across all segments, as shown by consistent quarterly growth rates (25-31%) and segment revenue increases matching management's breakdown.","evidence":["E13","E1","E43","E27","E28","E29","E30"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation fits the numbers","confidence":0.92}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":1,"rulingIndex":3,"finding_index":3,"ruling":"fits","reason":"Management attributes revenue growth to demand, not shipment timing. The quarterly growth rates are steady (25-31% each quarter), and segment growth is broad-based. The Q4 DSO increase (28→34 days) implies ~6 extra days of sales in receivables; at Q4 run-rate this equals ~$65-78M, or 7-9% of the $878.9M total growth. This minor potential pull-forward does not contradict the conclusion that the vast majority of growth is demand-driven, especially given the consistent quarterly pattern.","evidence":["E13","E1","E43","E27","E28","E29","E30","E50"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":3,"innocent_explanation":"Any revenue pull-forward from shipment timing is minimal (estimated $65-78M, 7-9% of total growth) and does not alter the conclusion that the vast majority of revenue growth is demand-driven, as evidenced by steady quarterly growth across all segments.","evidence":["E30","E13","E1","E43","E50"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation fits the numbers","confidence":0.92}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1336917_2015-12-31","revisionId":"ac7482310bc9","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":0,"finding_index":0,"ruling":"fits","reason":"Segment revenue increases (North America +$659.3M, International +$185.4M, Connected Fitness +$34.2M) sum to the total $878.9M revenue increase; each segment's growth rate is visible in the reported segment sales figures.","evidence":["E1","E13","E43","E45","E25"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":0,"innocent_explanation":"Segment revenue growth is directly visible in the reported numbers: North America (+$659.3M), International (+$185.4M), and Connected Fitness (+$34.2M) sum to the total $878.9M increase, with each segment's growth rate (23.6%, 69%, 178%) corroborated by the disclosed segment figures.","evidence":["E13","E1","E43","E25"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.8}}],"audit":[{"seq":1,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E1 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":10,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E10 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":11,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E11 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":12,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E12 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":13,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E13 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":14,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E14 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":15,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E15 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":16,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E16 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":17,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E17 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":18,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E18 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":19,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E19 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":74,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E1 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":75,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001336917-15-000006 -[supports]-> evidence:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":92,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9:E10 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":93,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001336917-15-000006 -[supports]-> evidence:1336917_2015-12-31:ac7482310bc9